1
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:17,750
Let the banquet of slaughter begin.

2
00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:20,920
Crush them all, Archfiend Ragnarok!

3
00:00:26,460 --> 00:00:28,220
A rose that blooms in the sky...

4
00:00:28,220 --> 00:00:29,630
A bat enveloped in flames...

5
00:00:29,630 --> 00:00:32,100
A band of light that razes the earth...

6
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:34,350
Each of these things is really quite rare.

7
00:00:35,180 --> 00:00:36,810
But they are unsightly.

8
00:00:38,020 --> 00:00:38,020


9
00:00:42,190 --> 00:00:42,980
Lady Alpha...

10
00:00:43,440 --> 00:00:45,690
We have an urgent report from Oriana.

11
00:00:45,690 --> 00:00:47,610
The Black Rose has activated.

12
00:00:51,070 --> 00:00:53,780
The destruction 
that precedes creation has begun.

13
00:00:54,410 --> 00:00:56,910
Wanna send out a ship?

14
00:00:57,160 --> 00:00:59,410
The city'll probably fall 
before it gets there, though.

15
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:03,750
That's all right. It'll work out.

16
00:01:04,670 --> 00:01:06,460
After all, <i>he's</i> there.

17
00:01:18,100 --> 00:01:22,650
Even considering you had the element of surprise, 
I'm impressed you managed to injure Ragnarok.

18
00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:25,650
I wonder who might you be.

19
00:01:30,820 --> 00:01:32,490
We are Shadow Garden.

20
00:01:32,820 --> 00:01:35,990
They who lurk in the shadows 
in order to hunt the shadows.

21
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:46,790
Go.

22
00:01:47,380 --> 00:01:50,050
There are things 
you must accomplish, do you not?

23
00:01:51,010 --> 00:01:51,970
Yes, my lord!

24
00:02:10,650 --> 00:02:13,110
You've overestimated your own power.

25
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:14,950
What a fool.

26
00:02:14,950 --> 00:02:17,410
I hope this teaches you to know your place.

27
00:02:17,410 --> 00:02:19,990
We'll see who the fool is soon enough.

28
00:02:20,830 --> 00:02:22,460
I believe this is our first meeting,

29
00:02:22,460 --> 00:02:26,790
Sir Mordred, Knight Beyond Men, 
Ninth Seat of Rounds?

30
00:02:27,130 --> 00:02:29,880
We haven't known each other long, 
but we're here to kill you.

31
00:02:29,880 --> 00:02:32,760
But first, we're going to need you 
to confirm some things for us.

32
00:02:32,760 --> 00:02:34,970
Lowly guinea pigs.

33
00:02:35,220 --> 00:02:37,430
I told you to learn your place.

34
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:42,020
An invisible sword stroke...

35
00:02:42,350 --> 00:02:43,560
I see.

36
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:45,980
So that's why they call you 
the Knight Beyond Men.

37
00:02:46,270 --> 00:02:47,690
Indeed, it is.

38
00:02:47,690 --> 00:02:50,320
My fencing style 
cannot be seen by mortal eyes.

39
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:52,530
I am impressed you managed 
to dodge a single strike—

40
00:02:52,530 --> 00:02:53,990
The Invisible Blade...

41
00:02:54,900 --> 00:02:58,240
An ancient elven artifact 
that unleashes an unseeable sword.

42
00:02:58,240 --> 00:03:00,990
Bragging about a stolen achievement...

43
00:03:00,990 --> 00:03:03,750
I suppose that's par for the course 
for the Cult of Diablos.

44
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:06,920
Are your armor and cape artifacts, as well?

45
00:03:06,920 --> 00:03:08,790
My, what a coward you are.

46
00:03:09,210 --> 00:03:11,630
Out of grief for our dying homeland,

47
00:03:11,630 --> 00:03:14,800
an elven swordsmith risked life and limb 
to forge that blade.

48
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:16,220
We'll be taking it back now.

49
00:03:16,680 --> 00:03:18,180
Mind your tongue!

50
00:03:20,390 --> 00:03:21,260
What?!

51
00:03:23,310 --> 00:03:24,600
A blade of magical energy!

52
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:26,850
An artifact I don't know about?

53
00:03:26,850 --> 00:03:31,570
The Wisdom we have been granted 
is beyond anything one of your ilk can comprehend.

54
00:03:31,570 --> 00:03:34,530
Now, share with us 
all of your musty knowledge.

55
00:03:34,820 --> 00:03:37,860
Things might start to sting 
a little if you refuse.

56
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:39,870
Foolish peasants!

57
00:03:39,870 --> 00:03:41,620
You think you can hurt me?!

58
00:03:42,080 --> 00:03:44,160
We don't stand a chance! Run!

59
00:03:44,160 --> 00:03:46,410
Going 'round in circles won't help!

60
00:03:56,260 --> 00:03:58,340
That was the last one inside the castle!

61
00:03:59,090 --> 00:03:59,970
What about in town?

62
00:04:07,770 --> 00:04:09,940
I'll just have to trust them to handle it.

63
00:04:09,940 --> 00:04:11,060
Princess Rose!

64
00:04:11,400 --> 00:04:13,610
Margaret, are you all right?

65
00:04:13,610 --> 00:04:15,030
Yes! Um...

66
00:04:15,230 --> 00:04:16,740
Princess Rose, I—

67
00:04:16,740 --> 00:04:18,530
I'm glad you're here, Margaret.

68
00:04:18,530 --> 00:04:20,490
I need you to unlock the cellar 
under the garden.

69
00:04:20,490 --> 00:04:23,030
It should be sturdy since 
it was built in ancient times..

70
00:04:23,030 --> 00:04:25,290
The castle residents can take refuge there.

71
00:04:26,200 --> 00:04:29,080
I will rally the knights 
and lead them into town.

72
00:04:29,080 --> 00:04:33,090
We have to at least do whatever we can 
to rescue the citizens.

73
00:04:34,300 --> 00:04:35,510
Is something wrong?

74
00:04:37,130 --> 00:04:37,920
No.

75
00:04:38,420 --> 00:04:40,510
I hear and I obey.

76
00:04:40,510 --> 00:04:42,390
I will take care of everything here.

77
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:45,350
Please, do whatever you feel is right...

78
00:04:46,020 --> 00:04:47,310
Queen Rose.

79
00:04:55,150 --> 00:04:56,230
That's a fantasy world for you.

80
00:04:56,690 --> 00:04:58,860
Even their bats are ginormous.

81
00:05:00,320 --> 00:05:02,030
Yeah, this is a disaster.

82
00:05:02,320 --> 00:05:04,280
Insane magic, insane power...

83
00:05:04,280 --> 00:05:06,700
This is what makes monster fights 
so impossible.

84
00:05:11,210 --> 00:05:12,830
You singed my bangs.

85
00:05:12,830 --> 00:05:16,300
With stuff like this, you wanna start by hitting hard, 
then just go with the flow.

86
00:05:16,300 --> 00:05:18,760
Didn't you learn that in school?

87
00:05:22,260 --> 00:05:24,180
The skies are under my control.

88
00:05:24,640 --> 00:05:25,930
Savage beast,

89
00:05:25,930 --> 00:05:27,930
let that truth be carved into your soul!

90
00:05:31,140 --> 00:05:32,230
That's it, then.

91
00:05:32,230 --> 00:05:33,230
You can do it!

92
00:05:33,230 --> 00:05:34,980
Yes, good luck to us all.

93
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:38,110
Status on the evacuation?

94
00:05:38,110 --> 00:05:40,950
We are currently organizing 
a search-and-rescue team to send into town.

95
00:05:41,200 --> 00:05:45,200
But about your orders to let them handle 
the magical creatures...

96
00:05:45,580 --> 00:05:49,080
Are you really sure 
we can trust these people?

97
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:53,580
If we have proven our worth to them.

98
00:05:54,330 --> 00:05:58,210
And I am certain we can do that 
by spilling our own blood.

99
00:05:59,010 --> 00:06:00,260
Now is the time to act.

100
00:06:00,260 --> 00:06:01,090
Yes, my queen!

101
00:06:03,470 --> 00:06:06,300
Shadow is fighting Ragnarok.

102
00:06:07,560 --> 00:06:10,060
As for the man called Mordred...

103
00:06:13,100 --> 00:06:14,480
Mordred?

104
00:06:15,270 --> 00:06:16,690
But how?

105
00:06:16,690 --> 00:06:18,150
I see you're working hard.

106
00:06:18,980 --> 00:06:21,190
L-Lady Beta, and...

107
00:06:21,190 --> 00:06:22,650
Epsilon.

108
00:06:22,650 --> 00:06:25,110
Damn, to think you'd be this strong...

109
00:06:26,280 --> 00:06:28,280
Bested by a pair of little girls...

110
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:31,660
Please don't try to tell me you only lost 
because it was two against one.

111
00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:36,580
It was foolish of you to rely on your toys 
when you knew you were at a numerical disadvantage.

112
00:06:37,590 --> 00:06:38,840
It's not over yet!

113
00:06:38,840 --> 00:06:40,670
I still have Ragnarok!

114
00:06:40,670 --> 00:06:43,920
With the greatest power 
ever recorded at my command,

115
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:46,720
I can take down the likes of you 
in a single instant!

116
00:06:47,090 --> 00:06:50,010
That instant seems awfully far away.

117
00:06:50,010 --> 00:06:52,640
If that's what you want, 
we'd be happy to wait.

118
00:06:53,100 --> 00:06:55,980
In the meantime, 
we hope you'll confirm some things for us.

119
00:06:55,980 --> 00:06:57,230
What?

120
00:06:57,230 --> 00:06:58,900
We told you earlier, remember?

121
00:06:58,900 --> 00:07:01,360
You should start telling us 
everything you know.

122
00:07:01,690 --> 00:07:06,110
About the Black Rose, 
the magical beasts, and the Cult.

123
00:07:06,490 --> 00:07:08,410
And you think I'll tell you?

124
00:07:08,410 --> 00:07:12,700
If you're so sure that Ragnarok is going to beat us, 
then where's the harm, right?

125
00:07:12,700 --> 00:07:14,410
Or are you scared?

126
00:07:14,410 --> 00:07:17,790
Afraid that your precious research specimen 
might be defeated?

127
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:20,210
Very well.

128
00:07:21,300 --> 00:07:25,220
In the very brief moments 
before Ragnarok incinerates you,

129
00:07:25,220 --> 00:07:28,090
I will allow you to be auditing students 
of my sagacity.

130
00:07:29,550 --> 00:07:34,770
Surely you're already aware that 
outside of our world exist countless other worlds.

131
00:07:34,770 --> 00:07:37,810
You're not talking about space 
and other planets, are you?

132
00:07:37,810 --> 00:07:40,440
I'm referring to different dimensions.

133
00:07:40,440 --> 00:07:44,740
We call the worlds that exist 
in those dimensions as Realms.

134
00:07:45,320 --> 00:07:48,910
For example, there's a world of ice 
that extends to the ends of the earth...

135
00:07:48,910 --> 00:07:51,160
A world of poison 
where no living thing can survive...

136
00:07:51,160 --> 00:07:53,160
A burning world of flame...

137
00:07:53,160 --> 00:07:56,290
A world of death with every inch 
covered by colorless tombstones...

138
00:07:57,210 --> 00:08:00,880
And a world inhabited by beasts 
that possess enormous magical powers.

139
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:08,800
These various realms revolve around 
a certain single point.

140
00:08:08,800 --> 00:08:12,720
And our world, too,
 is one of the worlds orbiting that center.

141
00:08:12,720 --> 00:08:14,350
What's at the center?

142
00:08:14,350 --> 00:08:15,560
Who knows?

143
00:08:15,560 --> 00:08:17,100
Perhaps some sort of god.

144
00:08:17,100 --> 00:08:19,270
Which is to say, you haven't 
been able to observe it.

145
00:08:19,270 --> 00:08:22,610
I am merely saying we are currently 
in the process of observing it.

146
00:08:23,480 --> 00:08:25,990
Stop making idle comments during my lesson.

147
00:08:26,740 --> 00:08:29,240
What lies at the center isn't important now.

148
00:08:29,700 --> 00:08:33,370
The problem is that countless worlds 
revolve around it.

149
00:08:33,370 --> 00:08:38,660
Around and around, for months, for years, 
the worlds follow their courses.

150
00:08:38,660 --> 00:08:40,620
Occasionally, they collide.

151
00:08:40,620 --> 00:08:44,960
When they do, 
the differing worlds become connected.

152
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:48,970
Allow me to give you an example 
of what could happen as a result.

153
00:08:48,970 --> 00:08:51,930
We once studied 
the ancient strata of our planet

154
00:08:51,930 --> 00:08:56,720
and discovered that, before a certain period, 
magic did not exist in this world.

155
00:08:56,720 --> 00:08:58,730
And when was that?

156
00:08:58,730 --> 00:09:01,770
Exactly when our world 
collided with a Realm.

157
00:09:01,770 --> 00:09:05,900
In other words, magic flowed 
into our world from that Realm.

158
00:09:05,900 --> 00:09:10,400
As a result, our world's biosphere 
underwent a dramatic change.

159
00:09:11,030 --> 00:09:13,780
And that led to the decline of the dragons.

160
00:09:13,780 --> 00:09:17,080
Exactly ten million years ago.

161
00:09:17,080 --> 00:09:21,420
They couldn't adapt to the magic 
that flowed into our world from the other.

162
00:09:21,420 --> 00:09:25,090
And those that could adapt 
to the new environment

163
00:09:25,090 --> 00:09:27,800
began to flourish in the dragons' stead.

164
00:09:27,800 --> 00:09:29,630
The humanoid races...

165
00:09:29,630 --> 00:09:33,340
But a certain question remains 
about this theory.

166
00:09:33,340 --> 00:09:40,890
Could it be that we humans too, 
like the magic and its creatures, came here from other worlds?

167
00:09:40,890 --> 00:09:42,190
Humans, too?

168
00:09:42,190 --> 00:09:45,860
There are still unanswered questions 
about the human race.

169
00:09:46,150 --> 00:09:49,820
We are the only species with this much intellect 
that have managed to thrive.

170
00:09:49,820 --> 00:09:51,110
We're different.

171
00:09:51,110 --> 00:09:54,700
Could we really, 
truly be inhabitants of this world?

172
00:09:55,570 --> 00:09:57,790
Magical creatures, magical power...

173
00:09:57,790 --> 00:10:00,410
The various humanoid races 
that have command over them...

174
00:10:00,410 --> 00:10:04,750
Since ancient times, all of these things and more 
have come into this world from other Realms.

175
00:10:04,750 --> 00:10:10,050
But in that same vein, some things have gone out 
of this world into those other Realms.

176
00:10:10,050 --> 00:10:11,380
You mean, spirited away.

177
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:13,220
Exactly.

178
00:10:13,590 --> 00:10:18,600
Once upon a time, there was an island kingdom 
that vanished without a trace.

179
00:10:19,010 --> 00:10:21,230
That kingdom was called Atlantis.

180
00:10:21,230 --> 00:10:22,810
Where do you think it went?

181
00:10:23,190 --> 00:10:24,730
To a Realm?

182
00:10:24,730 --> 00:10:27,150
This is an empirically proven fact.

183
00:10:27,150 --> 00:10:30,690
This world and the Realms 
are influencing each other equally.

184
00:10:31,070 --> 00:10:34,410
Then, did the Demon Diablos come from 
one of these Realms?

185
00:10:34,410 --> 00:10:38,990
That being was most certainly 
a product of our own world.

186
00:10:39,450 --> 00:10:41,620
But its original was not.

187
00:10:42,040 --> 00:10:46,630
The creature that became the basis 
for the Demon Diablos was a visitor from a Realm.

188
00:10:46,630 --> 00:10:51,010
We call that world the First Realm.

189
00:10:51,420 --> 00:10:52,840
First?

190
00:10:52,840 --> 00:10:55,550
We gained several pieces of wisdom from him.

191
00:10:55,550 --> 00:10:57,470
<i>That</i> is one of them.

192
00:10:57,800 --> 00:11:01,310
Surely, now you realize what it is.

193
00:11:01,310 --> 00:11:04,440
An artificial gate to another Realm.

194
00:11:04,770 --> 00:11:08,650
The Oriana Kingdom once opened 
that gate by coincidence

195
00:11:08,650 --> 00:11:12,940
and destroyed the hundred thousand Velgaltan soldiers 
that surrounded its capital in a single night.

196
00:11:13,650 --> 00:11:16,490
But this kingdom did not come out 
of that encounter unscathed.

197
00:11:16,490 --> 00:11:21,120
Magical creatures continued to spill out of the gate, 
devouring any humans in their path.

198
00:11:21,580 --> 00:11:25,620
And we came to their rescue 
by closing the gate.

199
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:31,340
So, doesn't it only stand to reason 
that you would pay the price?

200
00:11:31,710 --> 00:11:33,630
Royal blood...

201
00:11:33,630 --> 00:11:35,220
In this generation, that means you.

202
00:11:36,010 --> 00:11:39,550
Your blood, which is especially high in magic 
even for royalty,

203
00:11:39,550 --> 00:11:42,770
should have been offered to the Cult 
when you were an infant.

204
00:11:43,020 --> 00:11:45,680
But your foolish king refused to do it.

205
00:11:47,020 --> 00:11:48,400
Father...

206
00:11:49,810 --> 00:11:51,900
You can see what happened as a result.

207
00:11:52,360 --> 00:11:55,860
His ridiculous parental affection 
has destroyed Oriana.

208
00:11:55,860 --> 00:11:59,110
Next time, we'll endeavor to build 
a somewhat better kingdom.

209
00:11:59,950 --> 00:12:01,620
I won't let you!

210
00:12:01,620 --> 00:12:02,950
I will carry on my father's—

211
00:12:02,950 --> 00:12:05,370
That is for <i>us</i> to decide.

212
00:12:05,700 --> 00:12:10,460
You lowly guinea pig puppets 
have no say in the matter.

213
00:12:10,460 --> 00:12:14,210
You and Oriana will soon be no more, 
destroyed by Ragnarok,

214
00:12:14,210 --> 00:12:16,380
the Grand Ruler of the Fourth Realm—

215
00:12:19,680 --> 00:12:21,220
The Grand Ruler's arm?

216
00:12:34,020 --> 00:12:36,400
No, it's impossible!

217
00:12:36,740 --> 00:12:39,780
It can't be! That was Ragnarok!

218
00:12:39,780 --> 00:12:42,450
The being of the greatest level of magic 
ever witnessed!

219
00:12:42,990 --> 00:12:43,990
And he...

220
00:12:43,990 --> 00:12:47,160
That's impossible! It just can't happen!

221
00:12:47,160 --> 00:12:49,420
None of this makes sense!

222
00:12:49,420 --> 00:12:51,000
A living wonder of the world!

223
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:53,630
The greatest treasure of all the dimensions!

224
00:12:54,090 --> 00:12:55,210
Poor guy.

225
00:12:54,130 --> 00:12:58,300
That was the vessel 
capable of becoming the new prime field!

226
00:12:55,210 --> 00:12:58,050
If he understood even the tiniest fraction 
of the Wisdom of the Shadows,

227
00:12:58,050 --> 00:13:00,090
this never would've happened.

228
00:12:58,300 --> 00:13:00,430
The potential was there!

229
00:13:00,430 --> 00:13:05,100
Our theory could have been realized!

230
00:13:00,880 --> 00:13:02,050
Reporting.

231
00:13:02,390 --> 00:13:05,390
We've exterminated 
all magical beasts in the area.

232
00:13:05,390 --> 00:13:06,600
Good work.

233
00:13:06,600 --> 00:13:08,520
Let's split our troops, as planned.

234
00:13:08,890 --> 00:13:11,480
One to monitor the Rose, 
the other to assess the surrounding area.

235
00:13:11,850 --> 00:13:14,860
I'm especially concerned about what 
the rebel forces are doing.

236
00:13:17,530 --> 00:13:20,240
I must be tired. It's all just a dream.

237
00:13:20,240 --> 00:13:25,280
Apparently, I have a lot of stress built up 
from associating with these barbarians!

238
00:13:25,280 --> 00:13:27,950
Otherwise, I wouldn't be 
having this nightmare!

239
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:37,000
That was fun, 
like fighting a boss in a video game.

240
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:41,130
But Rose, Mr. Perv, or even any 
of the main characters were total no-shows.

241
00:13:41,130 --> 00:13:44,220
I need to get a little closer 
to the main storyline, at least.

242
00:13:47,510 --> 00:13:49,890
And now you're recycling 
the same special effects.

243
00:14:02,030 --> 00:14:04,530
Typical defect.

244
00:14:04,990 --> 00:14:04,990


245
00:14:10,200 --> 00:14:12,580
A defect?!

246
00:14:19,510 --> 00:14:20,170
Come on...

247
00:14:23,720 --> 00:14:27,100
Even the beasts are capable 
of recognizing a more powerful enemy.

248
00:14:27,100 --> 00:14:30,020
Think I'll be assigning you 
a rank below Delta.

249
00:14:42,110 --> 00:14:43,990
I've had just about enough of that!

250
00:14:49,910 --> 00:14:51,500
I'll kill you...

251
00:14:51,500 --> 00:14:55,620
I'll kill you!

252
00:14:57,130 --> 00:14:58,500
Where is he?

253
00:14:58,500 --> 00:15:00,590
Where did the bastard go?!

254
00:15:00,590 --> 00:15:01,380
They say...

255
00:15:02,340 --> 00:15:05,550
long ago, in order to chastise 
the humans on Earth,

256
00:15:05,550 --> 00:15:07,890
the gods unleashed lightning 
from the heavens.

257
00:15:08,800 --> 00:15:11,890
The people were fascinated by this power 
that rained down from the sky.

258
00:15:11,890 --> 00:15:13,230
They wanted it for themselves.

259
00:15:13,730 --> 00:15:15,390
"We need that power."

260
00:15:15,940 --> 00:15:18,360
"We must attain that power."

261
00:15:18,360 --> 00:15:20,150
Then, after much dedicated research,

262
00:15:20,150 --> 00:15:23,400
at last, the humans 
succeeded in obtaining it.

263
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:24,400
In other words,

264
00:15:24,400 --> 00:15:28,240
the nuclear energy between protons and neutrons 
that make up the atomic nucleus created fission,

265
00:15:28,240 --> 00:15:30,490
and the critical barrier...

266
00:15:30,490 --> 00:15:34,710
Or the exponent, or the function, 
or something, does a thing,

267
00:15:34,710 --> 00:15:36,420
and then, a chain reaction...

268
00:15:36,420 --> 00:15:39,540
Anyway, a buttload of energy 
creates explosive destruction.

269
00:15:39,540 --> 00:15:41,590
But nobody cares how it works.

270
00:15:42,300 --> 00:15:43,590
The far side of the heavens...

271
00:15:44,210 --> 00:15:48,010
The ultimate destruction, 
raining down from a soundless world...

272
00:15:48,010 --> 00:15:50,300
The extreme I must surpass...

273
00:15:51,220 --> 00:15:56,190
Seeing this place, feeling it, 
I realized again what I must do.

274
00:15:58,600 --> 00:16:00,980
I guess you'd call it, 
"Remembering why you started."

275
00:16:01,480 --> 00:16:03,150
And I owe it all to you.

276
00:16:03,530 --> 00:16:04,690
Thank you.

277
00:16:05,110 --> 00:16:06,570
So, this is it.

278
00:16:06,570 --> 00:16:08,110
I'm done playing.

279
00:16:08,740 --> 00:16:10,870
Because I wanna give this everything I have.

280
00:16:10,030 --> 00:16:10,870
Wait.

281
00:16:10,870 --> 00:16:12,410
I hope you'll accept my gratitude.

282
00:16:11,120 --> 00:16:11,950
Stop!

283
00:16:11,950 --> 00:16:13,540
What're you doing to me?!

284
00:16:13,540 --> 00:16:15,500
What the hell are you?!

285
00:16:17,410 --> 00:16:19,210
I'm Atomic.

286
00:16:20,210 --> 00:16:21,210
Huh?

287
00:16:37,980 --> 00:16:40,310
It's a little early for dawn.

288
00:16:40,940 --> 00:16:42,480
That must be...

289
00:16:42,900 --> 00:16:44,820
Yes, this is...

290
00:16:46,320 --> 00:16:47,530
So...

291
00:16:48,400 --> 00:16:50,410
this is what you've chosen.

292
00:17:05,710 --> 00:17:08,010
A polar light to dispel the darkness...

293
00:17:08,380 --> 00:17:09,760
But this is so...

294
00:17:09,760 --> 00:17:11,220
It's too much.

295
00:17:12,260 --> 00:17:14,180
My lord and master!

296
00:17:25,020 --> 00:17:26,650
Lord Shadow!

297
00:17:28,570 --> 00:17:29,320
Well...

298
00:17:29,780 --> 00:17:33,200
Every once in a while, it's not so bad 
to take the muscle-headed brute-force approach.

299
00:17:53,930 --> 00:17:55,720
What?!

300
00:17:56,220 --> 00:17:56,220


301
00:18:09,780 --> 00:18:12,070
<i>Looking at that moon reminds me...</i>

302
00:18:12,450 --> 00:18:14,240
<i>Of that day...</i>

303
00:18:14,240 --> 00:18:15,490
<i>Of him.</i>

304
00:18:18,370 --> 00:18:20,370
I must've fallen asleep.

305
00:18:22,960 --> 00:18:25,880
Why am I still wearing a uniform 
when I'm in my twenties?

306
00:18:27,500 --> 00:18:30,090
Miss Nishino, are you really going?

307
00:18:30,090 --> 00:18:33,090
Yes, I can't abandon my friends.

308
00:18:33,380 --> 00:18:35,760
But at night, they...

309
00:18:35,760 --> 00:18:37,300
I can handle it.

310
00:18:37,800 --> 00:18:41,890
Besides, I want to at least 
bring back some mementos.

311
00:18:44,730 --> 00:18:47,480
<i>There was a boy that I despised.</i>

312
00:18:47,980 --> 00:18:50,110
<i>His grades were just below average.</i>

313
00:18:50,110 --> 00:18:51,650
<i>Athletically, just below average.</i><i></i>

314
00:18:52,360 --> 00:18:54,700
<i>His looks were exceedingly ordinary.</i>

315
00:18:54,700 --> 00:18:57,490
<i>There was absolutely nothing 
memorable about him.</i>

316
00:18:58,200 --> 00:18:59,370
<i>And yet...</i>

317
00:19:00,410 --> 00:19:02,910
<i>Looking at that moon reminds me...</i>

318
00:19:02,910 --> 00:19:04,080
<i>Of that day...</i>

319
00:19:05,080 --> 00:19:06,290
<i>Of him.</i>

320
00:19:09,710 --> 00:19:11,340
<i>It's something I always knew.</i>

321
00:19:11,340 --> 00:19:15,680
<i>No one they attack 
has a chance of surviving more than a day.</i>

322
00:19:17,220 --> 00:19:18,800
It's getting late.

323
00:19:22,600 --> 00:19:25,520
<i>When was the last time I was alone?</i><i></i>

324
00:19:40,200 --> 00:19:41,910
I must be getting paranoid.

325
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:49,710
Aka-Akane N-N-Nishi-shi-shi, I presume?

326
00:20:07,100 --> 00:20:08,980
It's a new invention,

327
00:20:08,980 --> 00:20:11,480
supposed to suppress 
the oh-so-noble knights' powers.

328
00:20:12,150 --> 00:20:13,610
You know you shouldn't do that.

329
00:20:13,610 --> 00:20:18,030
Even if you are the great Savior, 
it's a bad idea to wander the streets alone at night.

330
00:20:18,030 --> 00:20:20,820
You might run into some unsavory characters.

331
00:20:20,820 --> 00:20:25,410
Now that we have... 
have you, we'll get the d-d-drugs...

332
00:20:25,410 --> 00:20:27,250
Or that's the cover story, anyway.

333
00:20:28,040 --> 00:20:31,000
What our client really wants is your life.

334
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:34,590
Seems like the Savior's made 
a lot of enemies.

335
00:20:35,130 --> 00:20:36,470
Enemies?

336
00:20:36,970 --> 00:20:39,430
Our client wants to do the honor 
of killing you personally,

337
00:20:39,430 --> 00:20:41,430
so we're supposed to bring you in alive.

338
00:20:41,850 --> 00:20:44,510
That's asking an awful lot 
in this day and age.

339
00:20:43,560 --> 00:20:45,140
Kill...

340
00:20:45,140 --> 00:20:46,390
Bad.

341
00:20:46,390 --> 00:20:48,810
Capture, get d-drugs...

342
00:20:50,650 --> 00:20:52,480
Calm down, brainless!

343
00:20:52,480 --> 00:20:55,110
You can get all the drugs you want 
when we hand her over!

344
00:20:55,110 --> 00:20:59,820
Girl... Hand her... 
Have her... Gotta have...

345
00:21:01,700 --> 00:21:03,490
He'll...

346
00:21:04,080 --> 00:21:05,790
He?

347
00:21:06,120 --> 00:21:08,120
He...

348
00:21:08,120 --> 00:21:09,710
Him...

349
00:21:11,210 --> 00:21:13,420
It's him!

350
00:21:14,040 --> 00:21:16,590
Kill! I gotta kill!

351
00:21:14,040 --> 00:21:16,590
Sorry about that, Great Savior.

352
00:21:16,590 --> 00:21:20,510
We've both had a lot of work done 
to the insides of our heads.

353
00:21:20,800 --> 00:21:24,470
He can't remember who he is, 
or what he was even doing.

354
00:21:24,470 --> 00:21:26,140
I can't get it out of my head!

355
00:21:26,140 --> 00:21:27,390
I can't get it out!

356
00:21:27,390 --> 00:21:27,930
That...

357
00:21:28,310 --> 00:21:30,390
That... That...

358
00:21:49,580 --> 00:21:51,000
He's here.

359
00:21:52,120 --> 00:21:53,290
It's him!

360
00:21:53,290 --> 00:21:56,590
It's the S-S-Sty... Stylish!

361
00:22:03,970 --> 00:22:05,010
Brainless!

362
00:22:05,010 --> 00:22:07,100
Stylish...

